<title>USA: U.S. Oct housing starts fell 5.1 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Oct housing starts fell 5.1 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce housing starts and</p>
<p>building permits, seasonally adjusted annual rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	October	September----Rev from--     Oct96/95</p>
<p>    -     Pct   Rate    Pct   Rate   Pct   Rate     Pct   Rate</p>
<p> Starts  -5.1  1,366   -6.1  1,440  -6.0  1,438     1.1  1,351</p>
<p> Permits -2.7  1,361   -1.7  1,399  -2.9  1,382    -2.3  1,393</p>
<p>October Starts and Permits By Region:</p>
<p>    -     Northeast    -Midwest-    --South--    --West--</p>
<p>    -     Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate    Pct  Rate</p>
<p> Starts  -9.3   127   -9.2   277   -8.3   604    6.5   358</p>
<p> Permits  Unch  138   -2.6   298   -2.6   588   -4.0   337</p>
<p>Seasonally Adjusted Annual Rates, in 1,000s:</p>
<p> Starts:     Oct   Sept--Rev from  Oct95</p>
<p> -Single   1,069  1,120  1,122     1,109</p>
<p> -Multiple   297    320    316	 242</p>
<p>Permits:</p>
<p> -Single   1,009  1,040  1,039     1,050</p>
<p> -Multiple   352    359    343	 343</p>
<p>Unadjusted Actual Starts and Permits, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	  Oct   Sept--Rev from   Oct95</p>
<p>  Starts     129    127    126	 126</p>
<p>  Permits    126    121    119	 122</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast October starts at a 1.443 million unit annual rate.</p>
<p>Department officials said the 1.366 million unit rate for starts in October was the lowest in a year since they were at a 1.351 million rate in October 1995.</p>
<p>The building rate for single-family homes was the lowest since 1.036 million a year in June 1995.</p>
<p>On the permits side, the applications rate of 1.361 million a year in October was the lowest since July 1995, when permits were running at a rate of 1.358 million.</p>
